{"name":"Montecito","hex":"#b6a180","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Montecito","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Santa Barbara County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Montecito"}],"entries":[{"title":"Montecito, Burnaby","blocks":[{"text":"Montecito, for administrative and planning purposes also known as \"Sperling-Broadway\", is a neighbourhood in Burnaby, British Columbia, Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Halifax_Street_Montecito.jpg/330px-Halifax_Street_Montecito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montecito%2C_Burnaby","wikidata":"Q6905039"},{"title":"Montecito, California","blocks":[{"text":"Montecito is an unincorporated town in Santa Barbara County, California, United States. Located on the Central Coast of California, Montecito sits between the Santa Ynez Mountains and the Pacific Ocean. Montecito is best known for its concentration of prominent and wealthy residents. In 2024, the median home price was $7.5 million. For statistical purposes, the United States Census Bureau has defined Montecito as a census-designated place (CDP). The population as of 2022 is approximately 8,638 residents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Casa_del_Herrero_%28Montecito%2C_CA%29.jpg/330px-Casa_del_Herrero_%28Montecito%2C_CA%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montecito%2C_California","wikidata":"Q1008912"},{"title":"Montecito (processor)","blocks":[{"text":"Montecito is the code-name of a major release of Intel's Itanium 2 Processor Family (IPF), which implements the Intel Itanium architecture on a dual-core processor. It was officially launched by Intel on July 18, 2006, as the \"Dual-Core Intel Itanium 2 processor\". According to Intel, Montecito doubles performance versus the previous, single-core Itanium 2 processor, and reduces power consumption by about 20%. It also adds multi-threading capabilities, a greatly expanded cache subsystem, and silicon support for virtualization."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montecito_(processor)","wikidata":"Q864328"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG/120px-Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG/250px-Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG/120px-Duthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADuthie_%40_Halifax_Montecito.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG/120px-Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG/250px-Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG/120px-Halifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalifax_%40_Duthie_Montecito.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Squint_Lake_Montecito.JPG/120px-Squint_Lake_Montecito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.or